body:
**What's wrong**

A `claude-*` model that a relay or a non-Anthropic subscription serves (kiro, 0-2kiro, cc, …) gets **no** auto-compact window from magpie: `~/.claude/settings.json` ends up with no `CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW`, no top-level `autoCompactWindow`, and no `modelSettings` entry. Since Claude Code 2.1.159 that means it never auto-compacts at all — a runtime guard added there gates autocompact behind an explicit window ([anthropics/claude-code#64520](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/64520)) — so a long session grows until every turn is a `400 Context window is full`, and the compaction request itself carries the same oversized history, so it can never shrink the conversation back (@99iii's log: ~26 consecutive 400s on `kiro/claude-opus-5-5`, the session file at 156 MB and each request body ~20 MB; the same session switched to `volcengine/deepseek-v4-1-flash` answers 200 at once, magpie writing it `272000`).

**Root cause**

magpie judged "one of Anthropic's own" by the model name alone (`claudeModel` — the `claude` prefix after any vendor prefix, plus Bedrock's `anthropic.claude` ids): at the four places compaction windows are decided — `writeCompact`'s env default and `desktopPlan`'s `work`, refs loop and top-level default — a claude-named ref was skipped as one Anthropic runs to its own window. That held while Claude Code auto-compacted by default; from 2.1.159 Claude Code needs an explicit window (its guard reads only `autoCompactWindow`/`CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW`), and for the prefixed id magpie hands it (`kiro/claude-opus-5-5`) it knows no window of its own — nothing managed the window at all.

**The fix**

`claudeOfficial` judges by the provider, not the name: true for a claude model on `api.anthropic.com` (the `anthropic` preset and the Claude subscription provider, whose Anthropic base it is), Bedrock or Vertex; false for a relay's or another subscription's claude model, and for a ref no provider of magpie's answers for (told a window, as any other model's). The four compaction decisions skip only an official one now: a relay's claude model gets the working window as any other model does, a threshold set on it or its provider first (#876), and a claude model on Anthropic's own endpoint keeps running to its own (#1741's `[1m]` case included — its test's provider is now actually a Bedrock one, which the name-only check never needed). Under the per-model budgets (Claude Desktop's plan) the working window serves as the top-level `autoCompactWindow`, so a model whose own is that one has no entry beside it — the same shape `claudePlan` already gives every model, values unchanged. Routing groups made only of claude models (`provider.ClaudeGroup`) keep today's behavior, as do the window-telling and output-token decisions that share the name check for other settings (`claudeWindow`, `claudeLongMain`, `claudeOutput`) — this patch touches the compaction half only.

Branch with the commit: [fix/5537-relay-claude-models](https://github.com/ggbdpq/magpie/tree/fix/5537-relay-claude-models) (head `2b490c28d171e7cc398b7b7db17c707628ef9939`), based on `416305451` (current `upstream/main`). Applies with `git am`.

